WEBVTT

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:23.790
<i>Every day I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:31.130
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:38.860
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:45.010
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:49.780
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:57.490
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:04.460
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:12.400
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:20.070
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:34.020
Somebody help me!

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:36.560
Please! Somebody
help!

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:39.820
Please help me!

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:40.990
Hmm?

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:43.160
Somebody help!

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:45.630
Please! Anybody!

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:47.170
What's this?!

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:49.570
Hang on, I'm
coming!

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.140
I hereby cast
judgment!

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:58.320
This is a no parking zone! Moreover,
it's a pedestrian sidewalk!

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:00.410
Parking on a sidewalk!

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.380
This is blatant and obvious disrepect
for parking regulations...

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:06.150
...not to mention that this phone booth
is blocked, trapping a girl inside!

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:07.760
This is unforgivable!

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.900
She thinks she's Ooka Echizen.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:10.030
"Ooka Echizen"; 17th century constable whose
adventures became a popular TV series.

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:12.960
In conclusion, I'm giving this
vehicle three parking tags!

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:16.290
And I'll pull it out of
the way myself!

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.920
This won't do.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:32.710
Hmm?

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:38.480
My poor MGF, it's blushing
red from all this attention.

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:44.360
Oh well, I can't blame you, as you
didn't know it was my car.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:45.300
Who's he?

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.490
Dunno...

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:50.470
Anyway, if you'll just remove
those tags and step aside.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:01.240
FILE. 33
WOW! CATCH1NG
AN IDOL STAR

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:06.510
Sure is a peaceful day.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:08.740
Yeah.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:15.190
Nothing could possibly go wrong
on a fine day like this, could it?

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.760
No.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:23.260
Look. Even the skylarks
are out and about.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:33.510
I knew it! It's
Tokki!

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:35.510
The singer, Tokio Katsuka.

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:37.480
Aah! Yoriko?!

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:41.850
Tokio Katsuka. Also
known as Tokki.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:45.150
Remember? All the excitement
when he won that F3 car race?

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.050
And the people who were hurt in a riot
at his concert? He's a pop idol!

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.990
He built a big mansion
in Beverly Hills...

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.500
He dates all the famous
actresses...

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.720
They even say he has
an illegitimate child!

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:58.740
You've got the whole
scoop, as usual.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.300
By now, you must have
realized who I am.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:03.830
So how about forgetting
those tickets...

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:06.200
Just who do you
think you are?!

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:10.700
Mr. Tokio Katsuka.
Lord Tokki.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:13.680
Get it? You
commoner!

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:15.450
H... Hey! Wait!

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:17.290
R... Regardless...

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.260
Lemme at him! Who does he think he is?!

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:20.750
Parking is not allowed on the sidewalk...

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:22.260
...so I'm giving you a
parking violation.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:26.130
Also, this street is closed
to traffic until 3;00 p.m.

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:36.130
Aren't you the
lucky ones?

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:39.400
All you have to do is write a ticket and
you get my autograph, just like that.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.740
Tokki! Over here!
Tokki!

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:45.320
Hey, it's mine!

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:46.680
Hey, it's mine!
No way, it's mine!

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:50.290
I want that ticket no matter
what anybody says!

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:54.890
No way! I want to frame
it for the locker room!

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:58.030
Tokkimania really is some-
thing to be feared.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.960
It is his own handwriting,
after all.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:04.190
Is he that
special?

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:11.900
Chief!

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:13.500
Are you going to
stand for this?

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:15.470
Well...

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:17.510
Well what?

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:20.180
The fact that he
autographed...

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:23.620
...or rather, signed the
ticket indicates...

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:25.520
...that he's willing
to pay his fine.

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:29.360
Beyond that, even Ooka Echizen
can't touch him.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:32.400
Hey...

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:42.560
Kobayakawa...

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:45.370
Yes, sir?

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.740
The next time you
catch that guy...

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:50.910
Yes, sir?

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:57.280
Get his autograph for me, would
you? My niece is a big fan.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.980
Chief!

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:10.460
It's been three whole days and we
still haven't seen that star.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:14.040
That's okay. We'll run into
him one of these days.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:16.440
Apparently, he lives somewhere
around here.

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:20.170
He'll be back. And he'll definitely
break the law again.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:23.250
Nakajima here. I've
found him!

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:24.720
Where?!

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:26.680
Where?!
I've got him here with me.

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:26.820
I've got him here with me.

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:28.680
He sure gets around.
I've got him here with me.

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:31.720
Whatever! Just tell
me where you are!

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.350
He ran a
light?

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:36.430
Yeah. But he stopped
immediately.

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:39.000
I was rather
surprised.

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:42.970
Come on, you guys.
This is no fun at all.

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:46.230
Don't you think writing tickets
is a little negative?

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:49.200
Let's be more
positive!

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:51.470
Shut your
mouth!

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:54.380
That's 2 points for
running a light.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:57.210
With all your priors, your license
is toast for 30 days!

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:00.380
Who's she, Tokki?

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:02.420
Probably a fan
of mine.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:04.580
She just wants to talk to me
because she likes me.

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.710
Don't mind her.

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:10.460
Talk about arrogance.

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:14.500
What... What did you say?!

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.470
What... What did you say?!
Cut it out, Natsumi! Calm down!

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:19.300
I know how you feel, but violence
isn't the answer.

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:23.500
Let me go! Please! Just give
me one shot at him!

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:25.580
Come on, Tokki. Let's
get out of here.

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:28.910
I suppose I should
pay my fine.

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:33.880
I'm sure they won't really
suspend my license.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:37.610
Hey, your bike's
in the way.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:39.420
How am I supposed
to get out of here?

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.350
Move it!

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:46.420
What did you say?! You keep
away from my bike!

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:53.500
Yeah, I was right.
It's been deleted.

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:54.310
"Fine Records"

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:57.240
Tokio Katsuka's traffic violations
have all been deleted.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:00.840
That's why he was so sure we wouldn't
suspend his license.

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:03.450
You mean that jerk was in here?

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:06.210
No, not at all. Think about it.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.220
You don't actually think he'd be
able to get in here, do you?

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:12.620
First of all, I don't think he'd even try,
and if he did, he wouldn't succeed.

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:15.020
On top of that...

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:18.290
...it'd be hard for him to
get into this computer.

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:19.830
So that means...

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:26.600
...he must have a powerful
friend here at the station.

00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:28.040
Holy smokes.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:29.970
We don't have proof yet, though.

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:32.110
Hey, Natsumi. Where are you going?

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:34.510
The washroom.

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:37.480
"Heartthrob Joins Traffic Safety Campaign"

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:43.390
Chief!

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:44.550
Y... yes?

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:47.060
I have to talk to you.

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:49.460
I have to talk to you.
I'm a little busy at the moment.

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:52.150
I'll wait here until
you're done.

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:53.920
Hurry up,
Chief!

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:55.460
She won't let
us through!

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:58.260
Don't rush
me.

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:02.570
Now I can't go.

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:10.080
Listen, the records couldn't
be deleted that easily.

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:14.950
Even so... The record of that
brat has been wiped clean!

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:18.190
Hmm... I see.

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:19.480
Well, how about
this?

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:23.150
Could someone have accidentally
erased them?

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:27.490
If that were the case, his wouldn't be
the only files that were deleted.

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:30.030
I suppose so.

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:36.200
Well, maybe one of his fans hacked into
the system, and took only his files...

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:41.250
Or not.

00:09:43.610 --> 00:09:45.670
Tsujimoto...

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:48.720
I don't want you making
too much of this.

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:50.710
Wha?

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:53.950
A... Are you telling me to turn
a blind eye to this?!

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:56.490
No! Nothing like that!

00:09:56.590 --> 00:10:00.050
We don't have any proof that anyone
is trying to cover up his record.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:02.960
But... on the other
hand...

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:07.470
You're the one person I never expected
to hear something like that from.

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:09.570
What I meant was...

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:11.230
Excuse me.

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:17.050
Uh...

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:35.500
"South District Magistrate"

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:40.640
<i>"Your honor! That's unfair!</i>
<i>I haven't done a thing!"</i>

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:42.900
<i>"Restrain yourself,</i>
<i>woman!"</i>

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:44.870
<i>"Cripes! It's Tokki!"</i>

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:48.780
<i>"Your outrageous attitude deserves</i>
<i>the ultimate punishment."</i>

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:52.370
<i>"You will be dragged around</i>
<i>the city, and then crucified!"</i>

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:58.380
<i>"That's not fair! I haven't</i>
<i>done anything! Huh?"</i>

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:02.390
<i>"Ch... Chief!"</i>

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:05.320
<i>"Do you expect me to turn</i>
<i>a blind eye to this, too?!"</i>

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:10.460
<i>"You traitor!"</i>

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:13.400
<i>"Take her</i>
<i>away!"</i>

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:16.410
<i>"Help me,</i>
<i>Chief!"</i>

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:18.480
<i>"Aah! Chief!"</i>

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:21.900
<i>"Chief!"</i>

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:32.650
How about saving the daydreams
for when you're off-duty?

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:35.750
That includes the
screaming, too!

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:39.660
My beloved Chief! How can I keep
him up on a pedestal now?!

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:44.020
No matter how much you like
the Chief, no one is perfect!

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:47.300
Anyway, there must be a
reason for his behavior.

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:50.910
Let's talk about that after Tokki
gets what he deserves.

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:55.740
I can't go on much longer,
feeling this way.

00:11:55.910 --> 00:11:56.580
Hey.

00:11:56.580 --> 00:11:58.640
Hey.
Hmm? Find something?

00:11:59.380 --> 00:11:59.480
"Tokki's Files"

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:01.650
Take a look at this.
"Tokki's Files"

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:03.990
Unbelievable!

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:06.560
This is full of details about
Tokki's personal life.

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:09.690
Check it out! Look at all
the women he's seeing!

00:12:09.990 --> 00:12:13.690
Who could have put all this
into the station database?

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:16.470
This is too
much.

00:12:17.030 --> 00:12:19.630
Tomorrow we have to
take care of Tokki.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:20.870
What?!

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:22.010
How's that?

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.070
It's the Traffic Safety Campaign.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:25.500
I know about
that...

00:12:25.610 --> 00:12:27.580
...but what does that
have to do with us?

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:33.110
The parade route was suddenly
switched to Bokuto precinct.

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:37.610
It starts out at the front of the
station then circles around.

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:41.620
I'm not crazy about the idea of
having a traffic outlaw...

00:12:41.790 --> 00:12:45.280
...heading up a campaign
for traffic safety...

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:48.370
...but having to protect him during
a parade is too much!

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:52.270
Huh? What is it? Are
you listening?

00:12:57.640 --> 00:12:58.880
This is it.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:01.740
This'll be our chance.

00:13:02.950 --> 00:13:04.240
Pardon?

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:13.280
Oh, Chief, could you round up everyone
from the Traffic Section?

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:16.520
We need help building the
stage for the ceremonies.

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:18.200
She's right, Chief.

00:13:18.200 --> 00:13:19.820
Okay. Will do.

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:21.760
All right! Let's do it!

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:24.230
Hip-hip hooray!

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:27.710
"Tokki's Traffic Safety Campaign"

00:13:27.710 --> 00:13:29.530
Hey, could you hand
me a nail?

00:13:29.710 --> 00:13:30.610
Here you go.

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:31.580
Thanks!

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:34.970
Here's where he lives. Here's
Bokuto Station.

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:38.150
Between them lie the train
station and some shops.

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:39.020
And?

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:40.540
According to Tokki's files...

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:46.520
...he always drives to his
gigs alone, in his MGF.

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:50.360
Tomorrow morning he'll be coming
here to Bokuto Station.

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:51.100
"The Press"

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:52.660
There'll be all kinds
of reporters here...

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:52.730
"The Press"

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:55.490
...covering the Traffic
Safety Campaign.

00:13:55.490 --> 00:13:55.500
"The Press"

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:59.530
I don't know how this
all came to be...

00:13:59.640 --> 00:14:02.370
...but I'm sure glad the parade route
was switched to our station.

00:14:02.970 --> 00:14:03.940
I get it.

00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:08.000
If he's caught in front of those cameras,
he can't cover it up or get away.

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:09.570
Yeah, but...

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:12.810
...we can't touch him until he
does something illegal.

00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:15.990
Don't worry about that.
I'm positive he will.

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:55.750
Great morning for
a little spin.

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:00.990
Huh?

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:03.960
Here he comes.
All right.

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:07.570
Huh?

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:09.600
Morning, officer!

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:11.870
You're out early!

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:15.500
Guess you have to, being
a public servant and all!

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:17.380
You go for it!

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:20.040
We'll just have
to respond.

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:24.410
Tinkerbell here. Captain
Hook, do you copy?

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:26.180
Captain Hook, over.

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:30.260
Peter Pan is coming your way. Repeat.
Peter Pan is coming your way.

00:15:30.430 --> 00:15:32.120
Roger.

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:38.870
Here he comes.

00:15:45.910 --> 00:15:50.040
Well, check this out. It's my two
biggest fans on the force.

00:15:50.150 --> 00:15:53.050
Stalking me so early
in the morning?

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:55.550
How about a
little race?

00:15:59.090 --> 00:16:00.120
Let's do it, Natsumi.

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:01.680
Let's do it, Natsumi.
Okay!

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:10.360
"Tokki's Traffic Safety Campaign"

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:15.530
I had to rush. At the last moment they
moved the schedule up 30 minutes.

00:16:15.710 --> 00:16:19.670
Yeah, but that's perfect timing for
the morning gossip shows.

00:16:20.110 --> 00:16:23.910
Hey, where'd Natsumi and Miyuki get
to?! We sure could use their help.

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:24.880
No kidding.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:29.250
You, in the MGF! Pull
over immediately!

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:35.550
It's an actor's gesture. Don't
take it seriously.

00:16:35.730 --> 00:16:37.160
Yeah, I know that.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:40.030
But still... Why
that?!

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:42.220
Time for a little
nitro!

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:54.680
What's with that
cop car?

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:57.270
Well, it's not going
to stop me!

00:16:57.880 --> 00:16:58.480
Miyuki!

00:16:58.480 --> 00:17:00.250
I know!

00:17:06.720 --> 00:17:07.950
Snot-miner!

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:13.960
You fool! I told you
to pull over!

00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:21.640
What the?

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:27.110
What a gas! Maybe I should consider
doing an action flick!

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:32.370
Oh, yeah?!

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:36.150
You'll have to get by me
first, if you think...

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:38.220
...you're coming
through here!

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:46.490
What?!

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:47.560
Bye-bye!

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:50.460
Oh, no!

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.470
It's going just
as planned.

00:18:06.320 --> 00:18:08.950
We're gonna settle this
thing once and for all!

00:18:09.050 --> 00:18:11.150
I'm getting out,
Miyuki.

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:13.290
Gotcha.

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:17.690
Here I go!

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:30.500
Thank you very much
for coming today.

00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:42.720
Stop, you selfish
fool!

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:44.990
Hello there.

00:19:01.670 --> 00:19:03.400
Thirty minutes
to go.

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:06.270
The press won't
be there yet.

00:19:06.380 --> 00:19:08.970
No one will have
a clue.

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:24.960
Oh my God!

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:38.460
W... What happened?

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:43.000
What's the press doing
here so early?

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:47.010
Well? How do you feel after your
little race, bright and early?

00:19:47.590 --> 00:19:51.390
Guess you'll be through
after this is aired.

00:19:51.720 --> 00:19:53.820
S... Sorry.

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:56.150
I cast judgment...

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:59.300
...upon thee!

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:11.560
The sudden request to change
the route and time like that...

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:14.840
You don't know how much
trouble it's caused.

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:17.840
We took every pre-
caution, sir.

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:18.880
Hmm?

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:20.780
Nothing, sir...

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:23.350
I'm very sorry.

00:20:23.520 --> 00:20:24.650
You should be.

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:27.720
You'll take the
heat for this.

00:20:44.980 --> 00:20:46.140
The files on Tokki.

00:20:46.310 --> 00:20:50.040
That's uh... my niece is in
his fan club, see, and...

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:53.880
...I just borrowed these
files from her.

00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:58.240
So you're the one who put those
files in the computer.

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:01.850
And? What does
that mean?

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:04.920
Chief!

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:09.330
I take back what I said about
you! I'm so sorry!

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:14.090
Forget it. But I haven't
done anything.

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:17.410
Don't waste your time with
frivolous investigations.

00:21:17.510 --> 00:21:21.470
And I'll take care of Tokki's
traffic records.

00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:23.000
Understood?

00:21:23.180 --> 00:21:24.170
Yes, sir!

00:21:24.280 --> 00:21:26.250
Thank you very
much!

00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:32.480
You're the greatest,
Chief! I knew it!

00:21:41.930 --> 00:21:44.400
You'll get burned...

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:46.490
...if you fall for me.

00:21:47.810 --> 00:21:49.770
Skylarks...

00:21:55.110 --> 00:22:00.620
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:03.620 --> 00:22:11.230
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:18.120
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:18.240 --> 00:22:28.250
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:28.310 --> 00:22:42.260
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:42.560 --> 00:22:50.500
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:59.040
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:22:59.310 --> 00:23:07.110
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:07.220 --> 00:23:16.680
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:17.090 --> 00:23:24.170
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:26.470 --> 00:23:27.730
"Stormriding the Iron Tower"

00:23:28.040 --> 00:23:30.810
It's awesome that we get to check
out traffic from the sky.

00:23:30.810 --> 00:23:31.940
Yoriko, don't get too excited!

00:23:31.940 --> 00:23:33.410
Isn't there something
interesting to see?

00:23:33.580 --> 00:23:36.940
As a self-standing iron tower
over 333 meters high...

00:23:37.110 --> 00:23:39.610
...the Tokyo Tower is among
the tallest in the world.

00:23:39.780 --> 00:23:43.510
At the 250 meter mark, there's
a special observatory.

00:23:44.190 --> 00:23:46.250
Next time, You're Under
Arrest, File 34...

00:23:46.420 --> 00:23:48.230
..."A 250 Meter-High Holiday."

00:23:48.230 --> 00:23:50.160
Ah! Chief!
